text = "[b]How it works:[/b]
Bubble Sort repeatedly steps through the list, compares adjacent elements, and swaps them if they are in the wrong order. The largest unsorted element \"bubbles up\" to its correct position after each pass. This repeats until no swaps are needed.

[b]Step-by-step example with [5, 3, 8, 1]:[/b]
[b]Pass 1:[/b]
  Compare 5 and 3 → swap → [3, 5, 8, 1]
  Compare 5 and 8 → no swap → [3, 5, 8, 1]
  Compare 8 and 1 → swap → [3, 5, 1, 8]
[b]Pass 2:[/b]
  Compare 3 and 5 → no swap → [3, 5, 1, 8]
  Compare 5 and 1 → swap → [3, 1, 5, 8]
[b]Pass 3:[/b]
  Compare 3 and 1 → swap → [1, 3, 5, 8]
[b]Done:[/b] [1, 3, 5, 8]

[b]Pseudocode:[/b]
[code]
FUNC bubbleSort(AR):
  [LET n = AR.length]
  [LET swapped = TRUE]
  WHILE swapped:
    swapped = FALSE
    FOR j FROM 0 TO n-2:
      [[IF AR[j] > AR[j+1]]:
        [SWAP(AR[j], AR[j+1])]
        [LET swapped = TRUE]
      ]
  [RETURN AR]
[/code]

[b]Time Complexity:[/b] O(n²) average/worst, O(n) best
[b]Space:[/b] O(1)
[b]Reference:[/b] [url=https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dsa/bubble-sort-algorithm/]GeeksForGeeks - Bubble Sort[/url]"
fit_content = true
